    "result_text": "The build is green. Done.\n\nI implemented the welcome notification on successful owner create:\n\n1. **New function** `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` \u2014 reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and emits `id=\u2026 memberId=\u2026` on the `NOTIFY` logger (mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern).\n\n2. **Wired into the pipeline** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `notifyWelcome` between `audit` and `respond`, so it runs only after the owner is successfully saved (the generated id and memberId are available) and before responding.\n\nVerification: the `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test (which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and memberId) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures. The observed log line confirms it: `NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
